From 61b0c239aa58a969afd74f1da73304029e98e022 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Mar 2026 00:54:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] SurfaceFlinger: Defer display mode changes until boot is
 finished

On GSI installations with multi-rate displays (e.g. 60Hz+120Hz), the
Scheduler selects the highest available refresh rate during init and
calls initiateDisplayModeChanges before the display pipeline is fully
operational. This calls setActiveModeWithConstraints on the vendor
HWC, which can break vsync delivery on older HWC implementations
that stop vsync during mode reconfiguration. Without vsync, no
frames are ever scheduled, resulting in a permanent black screen.

AOSP already defers resolution-changing mode switches during boot
(gated behind synced_resolution_switch). Extend this to defer ALL
mode changes until mBootStage == FINISHED. The Scheduler will
re-evaluate and apply the preferred mode once boot completes and
the display pipeline is stable.

This preserves the modeset_state_machine behavior while preventing
boot-time mode changes from breaking vendor HWC implementations.
---
 services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp b/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp
index 549d2a4..e8f03c2 100644
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp
@@ -1651,8 +1651,13 @@ void SurfaceFlinger::applyActiveMode(display::DisplayModeRequest&& activeMode) {
 }
 
 void SurfaceFlinger::initiateDisplayModeChanges() {
-    if (FlagManager::getInstance().synced_resolution_switch() && mBootStage != BootStage::FINISHED)
-            [[unlikely]] {
+    // [GSI] Defer ALL mode changes until boot is finished. On devices with
+    // multi-rate displays (e.g. 60Hz+120Hz), the Scheduler selects the highest
+    // refresh rate during init. Changing modes before boot is complete can break
+    // vendor HWC implementations that stop delivering vsync during mode
+    // reconfiguration, resulting in a permanent black screen. The mode change
+    // will be re-requested after boot when the display pipeline is stable.
+    if (mBootStage != BootStage::FINISHED) [[unlikely]] {
         return;
     }
 
